room warehouse "Harbour Loft"
  bg bg_warehouse_wide
  width 2560
  music music_office
  perspective horizon 250 ref 875 height 400
  # The crate stack on the left stands on the floor up to y≈790: walk only in front of it.
  # The ledger desk's footprint (x≈1060–1620) is notched out, so Fenn passes in front.
  walk (470,875) (520,795) (900,795) (910,705) (1060,705) (1060,840) (1620,840) (1620,705) (2380,705) (2500,875)
  entry 2280,800
  arrive alley 2280,800

  hotspot ledger "harbour ledger"
    show if not ledger_taken
    area 1210,470 270x130
    stand 1430,858
    look "The harbour ledger. Every arrival, every departure, every ship this town has ever lost, in one hand."
    open "The Arcadia: lost at sea, in Bramwick's hand, three days before she was even late. Beside it, a fee: “Paid, Cray & Co., factors.” Nobody pays harbour dues on a wreck. Bramwick didn't just write my father off. He was paid to."
      set ledger_read
      note ledger_read "The Arcadia was entered as lost at sea three days before she was due. Under the entry, a harbour fee paid in full by a factor's office. Nobody pays harbour dues on a wreck."
      sound chime
    use "The Arcadia: lost at sea, in Bramwick's hand, three days before she was even late. Beside it, a fee: “Paid, Cray & Co., factors.” Nobody pays harbour dues on a wreck. Bramwick didn't just write my father off. He was paid to."
      set ledger_read
      sound chime
    pull "It's chained to the desk. Of course it is."
    state if act 4
      look "The harbour ledger, still chained to its desk. The Arcadia's entry is where I left it: lost at sea, three days early, paid for by Cray & Co."
      open "I've read it. Reading it won't be enough; Cray's counting on that. The inquiry will want the book itself, and the book is chained to the desk."
        nothing
      use "I've read it. Reading it won't be enough; Cray's counting on that. The inquiry will want the book itself, and the book is chained to the desk."
        nothing
      pull "Chained. Bramwick chained it there himself, by regulation, so it could never go anywhere it might be embarrassed."
      pickup "It's chained to the desk. Regulation thirty-one, and a very good padlock."
    state if ledger_read = true
      name "harbour ledger"
      look "The entry still says lost. It will keep saying it until someone makes it say otherwise."

  hotspot crates "stacked crates"
    area 30,150 420x560
    nowalk
    look "More of Cray's cloud-stamped crates, stencilled for ports that ships have stopped reaching. Somebody is paying storage on a great deal of nothing."

  hotspot stairs_down "stairs to the lane"
    area 2400,300 160x460
    stand 2360,800
    exit alley
    look "The loft stairs, back down to the lane."

  hotspot chain "broken chain"
    show if act 4 and ledger_taken
    area 1210,470 270x130
    stand 1430,858
    look "A broken chain, and a clean oblong in the dust where the ledger sat for thirty years. Regulation thirty-one has been suspended, like its author."

  use crowbar on ledger if act 4
    "I get the crowbar through the chain where it meets the desk, and lean. The staple comes out of thirty years of oak with a noise like a held breath let go. The ledger is mine to carry."
    give ledger
    set ledger_taken
    sound pickup
